1
00:00:36,700 --> 00:00:38,039
I'm so sorry, Mr. Wan.

2
00:00:38,420 --> 00:00:39,560
I might be running a bit late.

3
00:00:39,560 --> 00:00:40,960
You'll have to wait for me a bit.

4
00:00:42,399 --> 00:00:43,200
See how it's done?

5
00:00:45,719 --> 00:00:47,600
Aren't you afraid he'll actually get mad?

6
00:00:48,100 --> 00:00:49,320
This is a pretty big order, you know.

7
00:00:49,780 --> 00:00:51,479
I've seen plenty of guys like him.

8
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:54,100
No matter how respectable they try to look,

9
00:00:54,320 --> 00:00:55,920
they're all just thinking about one thing.

10
00:00:56,280 --> 00:00:58,079
The more desperate he is for it,

11
00:00:58,299 --> 00:00:59,679
the blinder he becomes to the situation.

12
00:01:00,799 --> 00:01:01,479
Just watch.

13
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:02,439
Soon enough,

14
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:04,480
he'll sign the contract for me,

15
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:06,659
and obediently take me home.

16
00:01:07,180 --> 00:01:08,359
Is that any way to treat a dog?

17
00:01:08,420 --> 00:01:09,400
None of your damn business!

18
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:11,099
Why is he getting into a fight?

19
00:01:11,140 --> 00:01:11,879
Wait, wait!

20
00:01:12,579 --> 00:01:13,200
Not so hard!

21
00:01:13,439 --> 00:01:15,200
Ow, ow, ow!

22
00:01:16,780 --> 00:01:17,879
Aren't you a piece of trash?

23
00:01:18,099 --> 00:01:19,560
It just came begging for some food,

24
00:01:19,799 --> 00:01:21,640
and you burned its ear with a cigarette!

25
00:01:22,120 --> 00:01:23,920
Wait, what the hell do you want?

26
00:01:23,980 --> 00:01:24,659
Apologize to it.

27
00:01:24,700 --> 00:01:26,439
What? You want me to apologize to a dog?

28
00:01:26,439 --> 00:01:27,400
Are you out of your mind?

29
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:28,280
Are you going to apologize or not?

30
00:01:29,280 --> 00:01:31,879
I will! I will, I will, I will!

31
00:01:32,560 --> 00:01:33,120
I'm sorry.

32
00:01:33,299 --> 00:01:34,239
Sorry to who?

33
00:01:34,659 --> 00:01:36,599
How should I know what its name is?

34
00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:37,879
Then try them one by one.

35
00:01:38,019 --> 00:01:40,239
Niuniu, Wangwang, Beibei.

36
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:42,319
Try until it answers you.

37
00:01:42,420 --> 00:01:43,319
I'll try, I'll try!

38
00:01:43,719 --> 00:01:44,959
I'm sorry, Niuniu.

39
00:01:45,200 --> 00:01:47,079
I kind of understood him at first.

40
00:01:47,280 --> 00:01:49,159
But now I feel like he's just bullying the guy.

41
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:55,799
Bro Shan, Bro Tao!

42
00:01:55,859 --> 00:01:57,480
Save me!

43
00:02:07,579 --> 00:02:08,259
Stop!

44
00:02:08,460 --> 00:02:09,199
Don't run!

45
00:02:12,060 --> 00:02:12,800
Stop!

46
00:02:23,159 --> 00:02:23,919
What are you doing?

47
00:02:24,879 --> 00:02:25,759
Let's run.

48
00:02:26,300 --> 00:02:28,000
Alright, bride and groom, look at the camera!

49
00:02:28,199 --> 00:02:28,879
Ready...

50
00:02:29,120 --> 00:02:29,599
Go!

51
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:46,240
Run!

52
00:02:46,560 --> 00:02:47,680
Think you can get away?

53
00:02:48,080 --> 00:02:49,120
Stop right there!

54
00:03:09,099 --> 00:03:09,840
Where did this come from?

55
00:03:10,219 --> 00:03:10,960
It's his.

56
00:03:11,340 --> 00:03:12,080
Where's the guy who hit you?

57
00:03:12,159 --> 00:03:12,819
I don't know.

58
00:03:13,099 --> 00:03:13,659
Looks like he went that way.

59
00:03:13,659 --> 00:03:14,419
Alright, thanks, miss.

60
00:03:14,460 --> 00:03:15,120
Thank you.

61
00:03:16,500 --> 00:03:17,680
Is it those two by the road?

62
00:03:19,139 --> 00:03:20,280
I didn't scare you just now, did I?

63
00:03:22,280 --> 00:03:24,039
My dad used to be a debt collector.

64
00:03:24,360 --> 00:03:25,039
What do you think?

65
00:03:25,300 --> 00:03:26,080
What a coincidence.

66
00:03:26,740 --> 00:03:28,840
My dad used to be the one in debt.

67
00:03:29,159 --> 00:03:30,520
We're a match made in heaven.

68
00:03:33,560 --> 00:03:35,400
So, do you like puppies?

69
00:03:36,840 --> 00:03:37,919
They're alright.

70
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:41,280
They're just too pathetic.

71
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:43,680
They have a mouth full of sharp teeth,

72
00:03:44,159 --> 00:03:45,680
but all they do is wag their tails at people.

73
00:03:46,080 --> 00:03:47,280
To be honest,

74
00:03:47,479 --> 00:03:49,379
I was getting a bit annoyed waiting for you.

75
00:03:51,479 --> 00:03:52,699
I was wondering

76
00:03:53,259 --> 00:03:55,520
how long you were going to keep me hanging

77
00:03:55,860 --> 00:03:57,599
before you finally came downstairs.

78
00:03:58,960 --> 00:04:00,039
I was standing there getting annoyed,

79
00:04:00,219 --> 00:04:01,840
when I saw that chubby kid asking for it.

80
00:04:02,180 --> 00:04:03,580
So I took all my anger out on him.

81
00:04:06,939 --> 00:04:08,479
I actually quite like dogs.

82
00:04:10,960 --> 00:04:11,780
Good for you, then.

83
00:04:11,780 --> 00:04:13,360
Why are you smiling at me?

84
00:04:15,060 --> 00:04:16,079
I'm laughing because

85
00:04:16,500 --> 00:04:17,519
people like you actually exist.

86
00:04:18,139 --> 00:04:19,120
Are you

87
00:04:21,500 --> 00:04:22,379
complimenting me?

88
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:23,439
No.

89
00:04:24,660 --> 00:04:25,920
I find it a bit scary.

90
00:04:29,899 --> 00:04:31,120
I'm not selling the insurance anymore.

91
00:04:31,779 --> 00:04:32,839
Think about it yourself.

92
00:04:35,379 --> 00:04:36,439
Interesting.

93
00:04:39,660 --> 00:04:40,399
Wang Fenqi.

94
00:04:40,819 --> 00:04:42,279
I really don't think we're right for each other.

95
00:04:43,139 --> 00:04:44,879
Can you stop blowing things out of proportion?

96
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:46,480
I just said the navigation was wrong.

97
00:04:46,540 --> 00:04:47,839
Why wouldn't you believe me?

98
00:04:48,639 --> 00:04:49,600
And I also said

99
00:04:49,680 --> 00:04:51,360
we could take either of those roads.

100
00:04:51,839 --> 00:04:53,639
So even for something like choosing a road,

101
00:04:53,639 --> 00:04:55,399
it absolutely has to be done your way?

102
00:04:56,360 --> 00:04:57,339
The point is,

103
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:00,199
have I ever been wrong?

104
00:05:00,319 --> 00:05:01,620
So this is exactly why I said

105
00:05:01,620 --> 00:05:02,680
we're not right for each other.

106
00:05:02,740 --> 00:05:03,720
Neither of us can win,

107
00:05:03,800 --> 00:05:05,519
and neither wants to give in. In the end,

108
00:05:05,519 --> 00:05:06,139
Brake!

109
00:05:17,560 --> 00:05:19,480
I swear, you young people nowadays...

110
00:05:19,600 --> 00:05:20,759
are really something else.

111
00:05:21,279 --> 00:05:23,480
The severely injured carrying the lightly injured,

112
00:05:23,779 --> 00:05:25,439
yelling all over the hospital lobby.

113
00:05:26,240 --> 00:05:27,800
Do you realize you're about to go blind?

114
00:05:29,220 --> 00:05:29,800
What's next?

115
00:05:29,939 --> 00:05:30,759
Are you gonna demand

116
00:05:30,959 --> 00:05:32,000
that the one with superficial wounds

117
00:05:32,079 --> 00:05:33,199
gets put in the ICU?

118
00:05:33,360 --> 00:05:34,279
Is that what you want?

119
00:05:34,620 --> 00:05:36,040
I know I'm fine.

120
00:05:36,259 --> 00:05:37,360
But I don't know about her.

121
00:05:37,720 --> 00:05:39,279
Doctor, don't listen to his nonsense.

122
00:05:39,480 --> 00:05:40,279
He's always like this.

123
00:05:41,279 --> 00:05:44,079
How's his eye? Is it okay?

124
00:05:45,920 --> 00:05:47,879
We can't completely rule out the risks yet.

125
00:05:48,300 --> 00:05:49,560
We'll have to wait a couple of days to see

126
00:05:49,560 --> 00:05:50,759
how his body recovers.

127
00:05:51,699 --> 00:05:53,000
Just sit here for observation for a bit.

128
00:05:53,319 --> 00:05:53,860
Okay.

129
00:05:54,680 --> 00:05:55,680
Thank you, doctor.

130
00:06:17,560 --> 00:06:19,040
Wipe that smile off your face.

131
00:06:19,399 --> 00:06:20,759
Do you know you almost went blind?

132
00:06:22,439 --> 00:06:23,920
Don't think playing the hero

133
00:06:23,920 --> 00:06:25,439
will solve our problems.

134
00:06:25,680 --> 00:06:26,480
I'm not.

135
00:06:26,800 --> 00:06:28,360
I'm laughing at myself.

136
00:06:28,920 --> 00:06:30,279
If I really went blind,

137
00:06:30,420 --> 00:06:32,879
then my lifelong wish would come true.

138
00:06:33,199 --> 00:06:35,480
To be a pirate.

139
00:06:40,740 --> 00:06:41,680
Look what's ahead!

140
00:06:42,500 --> 00:06:43,279
Enemy ship over there!

141
00:06:43,439 --> 00:06:44,360
Quick, fire the cannons!

142
00:06:44,839 --> 00:06:46,000
Miss Mermaid here,

143
00:06:46,860 --> 00:06:49,079
want to be a pirate's wife?

144
00:06:49,439 --> 00:06:50,279
Do you?

145
00:06:50,620 --> 00:06:51,199
No.

146
00:06:51,480 --> 00:06:52,319
Stop messing around.

147
00:06:52,439 --> 00:06:53,680
I'm not. You're so annoying.

148
00:06:54,540 --> 00:06:55,439
There's no regret pill.

149
00:06:55,500 --> 00:06:56,279
I won't take one.

150
00:06:56,660 --> 00:06:57,560
I won't.

151
00:06:57,839 --> 00:06:59,319
You married him?

152
00:06:59,860 --> 00:07:01,259
You've only been dating for six months.

153
00:07:01,980 --> 00:07:04,000
No wonder you quit without a word.

154
00:07:04,240 --> 00:07:05,120
Did he make you quit?

155
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:06,079
So what?

156
00:07:06,480 --> 00:07:07,540
If it doesn't work out, we'll divorce.

157
00:07:08,060 --> 00:07:10,319
By the way, we're not having a wedding.

158
00:07:10,500 --> 00:07:12,120
But you still have to send a cash gift.

159
00:07:13,139 --> 00:07:14,240
I'm heading out soon.

160
00:07:14,459 --> 00:07:15,639
That's it, bye.

161
00:07:19,579 --> 00:07:21,360
What is all this junk?

162
00:07:23,399 --> 00:07:24,480
You're so uncultured.

163
00:07:24,939 --> 00:07:27,040
This is a handmade piece by Master Yilong.

164
00:07:27,500 --> 00:07:29,040
I made a small profit last week,

165
00:07:29,100 --> 00:07:29,959
so I picked it up.

166
00:07:30,620 --> 00:07:32,319
Just tell me how much money you wasted.

167
00:07:34,480 --> 00:07:35,639
This thing costs 5,000?

168
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:37,720
Does 5,000 even qualify as handmade?

169
00:07:39,959 --> 00:07:40,879
50,000.

170
00:07:43,500 --> 00:07:44,319
Wang Fenqi.

171
00:07:45,339 --> 00:07:47,120
I used to think you were quite smart.

172
00:07:47,360 --> 00:07:49,240
Why are you getting more and more ridiculous?

173
00:07:49,600 --> 00:07:51,920
Your cryptocurrency is like walking a tightrope.

174
00:07:52,060 --> 00:07:54,019
Don't assume you can always stride forward.

175
00:07:54,100 --> 00:07:55,680
Think about what you'll do when you fall.

176
00:07:56,259 --> 00:07:57,240
Let me tell you,

177
00:07:57,519 --> 00:07:58,839
the more you fear falling to your death,

178
00:07:59,100 --> 00:08:00,920
the faster you actually will.

179
00:08:01,500 --> 00:08:02,480
If you want to survive,

180
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:05,639
you have to gamble with your life.

181
00:08:15,060 --> 00:08:16,279
You heartless thing.

182
00:08:16,360 --> 00:08:17,959
You haven't visited me for months.

183
00:08:18,920 --> 00:08:20,319
I just wanted to ask...

184
00:08:21,560 --> 00:08:23,240
Are you guys acting as agents for

185
00:08:23,319 --> 00:08:24,639
an investment insurance from Hong Kong, China?

186
00:08:24,740 --> 00:08:25,319
Yeah.

187
00:08:25,660 --> 00:08:27,040
That's mostly for old folks.

188
00:08:27,100 --> 00:08:28,040
There's nothing special about it.

189
00:08:28,899 --> 00:08:30,000
Why? Do you want to buy it?

190
00:08:30,360 --> 00:08:33,639
Let me see the materials first.

191
00:08:36,960 --> 00:08:38,360
Are you guys doing okay?

192
00:08:40,019 --> 00:08:41,879
I still see his live streams sometimes.

193
00:08:42,679 --> 00:08:43,600
We're doing fine.

194
00:08:44,440 --> 00:08:45,320
I just figured...

195
00:08:46,399 --> 00:08:48,039
I'd better prepare for a rainy day.

196
00:08:49,159 --> 00:08:49,960
After all,

197
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:51,720
no one can win forever.

198
00:08:56,399 --> 00:08:58,039
The house is gone.

199
00:08:58,980 --> 00:09:00,559
He bet everything on it.

200
00:09:04,720 --> 00:09:06,279
We bought a retirement house

201
00:09:06,399 --> 00:09:07,679
out in the suburbs a while ago.

202
00:09:07,980 --> 00:09:08,759
See

203
00:09:08,919 --> 00:09:10,039
how much it can be mortgaged for.

204
00:09:10,440 --> 00:09:12,679
At least it can help you out a bit.

205
00:09:13,320 --> 00:09:15,279
Mom, put the property deed away.

206
00:09:16,240 --> 00:09:17,879
Giving it to him now is just hurting him.

207
00:09:20,940 --> 00:09:22,600
What he's doing isn't a business.

208
00:09:22,779 --> 00:09:23,759
It's just gambling.

209
00:09:24,399 --> 00:09:25,960
He's completely lost his mind right now.

210
00:09:26,259 --> 00:09:28,320
No amount of money can fill that hole.

211
00:09:28,799 --> 00:09:30,840
He's just too smart.

212
00:09:31,179 --> 00:09:33,120
He's never lost in his entire life.

213
00:09:33,600 --> 00:09:35,720
He doesn't know how to handle setbacks.

214
00:09:36,139 --> 00:09:37,240
We're really afraid

215
00:09:37,460 --> 00:09:39,279
he might do something drastic.

216
00:09:40,919 --> 00:09:41,679
Stop talking.

217
00:09:41,860 --> 00:09:42,720
What do you know?

218
00:09:42,919 --> 00:09:43,879
Let her speak.

219
00:09:44,220 --> 00:09:45,159
What are your thoughts?

220
00:09:45,320 --> 00:09:46,519
Since I married him,

221
00:09:47,179 --> 00:09:48,360
I'll stay by his side.

222
00:09:49,120 --> 00:09:51,360
I bought this investment insurance secretly.

223
00:09:52,059 --> 00:09:53,600
I'm afraid he'll find out about it.

224
00:09:53,960 --> 00:09:55,240
So let me keep it with you for now.

225
00:09:56,820 --> 00:09:57,879
If one day,

226
00:09:58,919 --> 00:10:00,279
he can regain his senses,

227
00:10:00,980 --> 00:10:02,159
I'll use this money

228
00:10:02,480 --> 00:10:03,639
to start over with him.

229
00:10:04,720 --> 00:10:06,360
That puts my mind at ease.

230
00:10:06,899 --> 00:10:07,860
In business,

231
00:10:07,940 --> 00:10:09,320
winning and losing is normal.

232
00:10:10,159 --> 00:10:10,759
By the way,

233
00:10:11,019 --> 00:10:13,559
that house in the suburbs is ready.

234
00:10:14,200 --> 00:10:15,159
Why don't you guys

235
00:10:15,799 --> 00:10:16,919
live there for now?

236
00:10:17,580 --> 00:10:18,720
And have a baby.

237
00:10:19,200 --> 00:10:20,320
With a baby,

238
00:10:20,600 --> 00:10:22,039
a man will become more mature.

239
00:10:22,299 --> 00:10:24,100
Mom, let's talk about this later.

240
00:10:24,879 --> 00:10:26,240
I'll tell him. I'll tell him.

241
00:10:27,600 --> 00:10:28,960
It's been hard on him too.

242
00:10:33,559 --> 00:10:35,720
My parents recently bought a house.

243
00:10:35,960 --> 00:10:37,840
You and An'an can live there for now.

244
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:38,840
Even if I starve to death,

245
00:10:38,840 --> 00:10:40,399
I won't spend a dime of your money.

246
00:10:42,399 --> 00:10:43,960
What did you say to my parents just now?

247
00:10:44,039 --> 00:10:45,639
Just about the house.

248
00:10:47,320 --> 00:10:49,039
I'm asking you what you said to them!

249
00:11:08,279 --> 00:11:09,919
Are you crazy driving this fast?!

250
00:11:10,299 --> 00:11:12,320
I asked what you told them!

251
00:11:13,480 --> 00:11:14,960
I said you've hated losing since you were a kid.

252
00:11:15,120 --> 00:11:16,360
That you're a sore loser.

253
00:11:28,340 --> 00:11:30,360
Three, two, one.

254
00:11:30,480 --> 00:11:32,480
Welcome home.

255
00:11:37,019 --> 00:11:38,860
Wang Fenqi, Mr. Wang, right?

256
00:11:39,259 --> 00:11:40,440
I'm a fan of yours.

257
00:11:40,720 --> 00:11:41,500
Want a picture?

258
00:11:41,799 --> 00:11:42,679
That won't be necessary.

259
00:11:43,039 --> 00:11:43,879
I'm just afraid

260
00:11:44,159 --> 00:11:45,759
it would dirty my phone.

261
00:11:46,419 --> 00:11:47,840
I was just curious and came to ask.

262
00:11:48,379 --> 00:11:49,539
You, Wan the Leek,

263
00:11:49,720 --> 00:11:51,460
ripped off so many people in crypto trading,

264
00:11:51,759 --> 00:11:52,399
so how come

265
00:11:52,639 --> 00:11:55,000
you've now sunk to joining us common folk

266
00:11:55,080 --> 00:11:56,320
in buying basic housing?

267
00:11:57,100 --> 00:11:57,759
Let's go.

268
00:11:59,639 --> 00:12:00,399
I don't live here.

269
00:12:00,519 --> 00:12:01,480
I bought it for my parents.

270
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:03,720
More like your parents bought it for you.

271
00:12:05,100 --> 00:12:05,759
Honey,

272
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:08,559
I have this client from before.

273
00:12:08,879 --> 00:12:11,000
He's been wanting me to arrange a meeting with you.

274
00:12:11,080 --> 00:12:13,019
Why don't you meet with him

275
00:12:13,159 --> 00:12:14,360
and help out at his company?

276
00:12:20,879 --> 00:12:21,759
What do you mean?

277
00:12:22,139 --> 00:12:23,480
Are you pitying me?

278
00:12:40,200 --> 00:12:41,759
What's wrong? What are you looking for?

279
00:12:42,259 --> 00:12:42,840
Got it.

280
00:12:49,879 --> 00:12:50,679
Let me ask you.

281
00:12:51,980 --> 00:12:54,039
The money I give you for your birthday every year...

282
00:12:54,879 --> 00:12:55,960
...what did you spend it on?

283
00:12:56,559 --> 00:12:57,799
How should I remember that?

284
00:12:58,299 --> 00:12:59,759
I just spent it all on random stuff.

285
00:13:00,240 --> 00:13:01,679
Your bags are all fake.

286
00:13:02,379 --> 00:13:03,879
And you haven't bought much jewelry.

287
00:13:04,279 --> 00:13:05,279
With all that money...

288
00:13:05,639 --> 00:13:08,220
...don't tell me you spent it all at the beauty salon.

289
00:13:10,220 --> 00:13:11,720
I really can't remember.

290
00:13:12,919 --> 00:13:14,580
Besides, once you transfer it to me, it's mine.

291
00:13:14,639 --> 00:13:16,200
I can spend it however I want.

292
00:13:19,940 --> 00:13:21,100
I'll ask you one more time.

293
00:13:21,259 --> 00:13:23,000
I just need you to tell the truth.

294
00:13:23,240 --> 00:13:24,159
That money...

295
00:13:25,519 --> 00:13:27,080
...what did you spend it on?

296
00:13:29,740 --> 00:13:30,840
I can't remember.

297
00:13:31,940 --> 00:13:32,960
You can't remember?

298
00:13:33,120 --> 00:13:35,200
I guess a leopard never changes its spots.

299
00:13:35,320 --> 00:13:36,519
You hid the money...

300
00:13:36,799 --> 00:13:38,600
...just to leave yourself an escape route, didn't you?

301
00:13:46,919 --> 00:13:48,399
Do you really distrust me that much?

302
00:13:50,100 --> 00:13:50,860
Say something!

303
00:13:51,240 --> 00:13:51,879
Where is the money?

304
00:13:51,940 --> 00:13:53,139
What did you spend all that money on?

305
00:13:53,139 --> 00:13:54,320
I don't know!

306
00:13:55,179 --> 00:13:56,480
Let go of me!

307
00:13:57,399 --> 00:13:58,419
What did you do with the money?

308
00:13:58,500 --> 00:13:59,139
Where is it?

309
00:13:59,200 --> 00:13:59,759
Tell me!

310
00:13:59,840 --> 00:14:00,480
Answer me!

311
00:14:00,480 --> 00:14:02,679
I don't know! Let go of me!

312
00:14:02,759 --> 00:14:03,399
Where are you going?

313
00:14:03,539 --> 00:14:04,419
Explain yourself!

314
00:14:04,620 --> 00:14:05,200
Don't walk away!

315
00:14:05,360 --> 00:14:06,240
Get back here!

316
00:14:10,139 --> 00:14:10,679
An'an!

317
00:14:10,840 --> 00:14:11,679
Are you okay?

318
00:14:21,159 --> 00:14:22,159
I didn't mean to!

319
00:14:38,600 --> 00:14:39,759
Whatever his reasons are,

320
00:14:39,879 --> 00:14:40,840
this is domestic violence.

321
00:14:40,899 --> 00:14:42,279
If he does it once, he'll do it again.

322
00:14:42,620 --> 00:14:43,960
With his extreme personality,

323
00:14:44,240 --> 00:14:45,639
he might even end up killing you.

324
00:14:49,259 --> 00:14:50,759
Look how old I am.

325
00:14:51,120 --> 00:14:52,480
I'm not some high school girl.

326
00:14:53,279 --> 00:14:55,200
Don't worry, I know what I'm doing.

327
00:14:56,740 --> 00:14:57,860
He saved me once,

328
00:14:58,519 --> 00:14:59,519
so I'll return the favor once.

329
00:15:00,019 --> 00:15:00,799
Just this once.

330
00:15:01,779 --> 00:15:02,759
The worst kind are

331
00:15:02,860 --> 00:15:03,440
the stupid ones.

332
00:15:03,620 --> 00:15:04,440
They run away at the first scare.

333
00:15:04,559 --> 00:15:06,440
Only the smart ones lose it all.

334
00:15:07,419 --> 00:15:09,360
Didn't I tell you when I got married?

335
00:15:09,559 --> 00:15:11,240
What's there to fear? At worst, I'll just get a divorce.

336
00:15:13,320 --> 00:15:14,639
I already told Old Liu.

337
00:15:14,840 --> 00:15:16,480
I'm going back to work next week.

338
00:15:16,740 --> 00:15:17,519
Really?

339
00:15:17,659 --> 00:15:18,480
Of course.

340
00:15:20,480 --> 00:15:21,679
I'm not that smart,

341
00:15:22,740 --> 00:15:23,720
but I'm not that stupid either.

342
00:15:27,840 --> 00:15:29,120
Welcome home.

343
00:15:47,720 --> 00:15:48,440
Get off me!

344
00:15:50,799 --> 00:15:51,559
What are you doing?

345
00:15:55,960 --> 00:15:57,279
Let me smell if you have

346
00:15:57,919 --> 00:15:59,879
another man's scent on you.

347
00:16:02,320 --> 00:16:03,240
Are you crazy?

348
00:16:07,059 --> 00:16:08,039
Cut the act.

349
00:16:08,879 --> 00:16:10,480
You're just getting older,

350
00:16:10,679 --> 00:16:12,539
so you don't sell as easily as you used to.

351
00:16:12,779 --> 00:16:13,480
Oh, really?

352
00:16:13,779 --> 00:16:14,360
Yeah.

353
00:16:15,039 --> 00:16:16,120
Even if I did go sell myself,

354
00:16:16,740 --> 00:16:17,879
it'd still be better than hiding at home all day

355
00:16:17,879 --> 00:16:19,320
just to save face!

356
00:16:24,960 --> 00:16:26,039
Say that again!

357
00:16:27,259 --> 00:16:28,120
Get away!

358
00:16:33,919 --> 00:16:34,600
Open the door!

359
00:16:37,480 --> 00:16:39,519
Bai An'an!

360
00:16:42,919 --> 00:16:43,879
Open the door!

361
00:16:45,600 --> 00:16:46,639
Open the door!

362
00:16:48,440 --> 00:16:49,480
Open the door!

363
00:16:51,179 --> 00:16:55,159
Open the door! Open the door! Open the door!

364
00:16:55,620 --> 00:16:57,799
Open the door! Open the door! Open the door!

365
00:16:58,559 --> 00:16:59,480
Open the door!

366
00:17:29,859 --> 00:17:32,319
Don't even think about escaping.

367
00:17:33,940 --> 00:17:35,960
Has your husband run into some trouble lately?

368
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:38,339
Do you still remember Mr. Wang?

369
00:17:39,640 --> 00:17:41,400
He asked for you by name.

370
00:17:42,220 --> 00:17:43,220
You can't rely on men.

371
00:17:43,220 --> 00:17:45,680
Women have to hold up their half of the sky.

372
00:17:46,740 --> 00:17:47,559
Drink up, and I'll sign.

373
00:17:48,019 --> 00:17:48,920
I won't go back on my word.

374
00:17:49,559 --> 00:17:50,559
Here's to you.

375
00:17:55,400 --> 00:17:56,440
If you don't like living here, get the hell out!

376
00:17:56,599 --> 00:17:57,599
Get out and go find your next one!

377
00:17:57,700 --> 00:17:58,799
Fine, I'll get out.

378
00:18:50,339 --> 00:18:51,759
I'm sorry.

379
00:18:52,380 --> 00:18:54,160
My partner will be back soon.

380
00:18:55,019 --> 00:18:56,960
I need to move you somewhere else.

381
00:19:35,799 --> 00:19:37,160
Have you seen the second-floor neighbor?

382
00:19:37,279 --> 00:19:38,859
No, no idea.

383
00:20:08,519 --> 00:20:09,640
Don't... don't be afraid.

384
00:20:09,940 --> 00:20:10,960
I'm almost home.

385
00:21:03,900 --> 00:21:05,160
There's something

386
00:21:05,880 --> 00:21:07,559
I've always found really strange.

387
00:21:08,019 --> 00:21:09,400
That Wang Fenqi...

388
00:21:09,660 --> 00:21:11,240
Such an important earring...

389
00:21:12,220 --> 00:21:13,599
he didn't give it to the police.

390
00:21:14,359 --> 00:21:16,160
He showed it to me instead.

391
00:21:18,799 --> 00:21:19,759
What earring?

392
00:21:44,940 --> 00:21:46,200
We need to move her right now.

393
00:21:47,319 --> 00:21:48,180
Move her where?

394
00:21:52,359 --> 00:21:53,160
Easy, easy.

395
00:22:32,339 --> 00:22:33,039
Turning it off.

396
00:23:19,720 --> 00:23:20,559
Give her another bottle.

397
00:23:21,480 --> 00:23:22,839
Her blood counts are still a bit high.

398
00:24:38,859 --> 00:24:40,359
I did it all myself.

399
00:24:40,740 --> 00:24:41,839
It has nothing to do with her.

400
00:24:42,559 --> 00:24:43,680
I'll turn myself in right now.

401
00:24:45,539 --> 00:24:46,640
We'll turn ourselves in.

402
00:24:47,420 --> 00:24:48,359
There's no rush.

403
00:24:49,940 --> 00:24:51,680
I already told your wife.

404
00:24:52,720 --> 00:24:54,000
We can talk this over

405
00:24:54,640 --> 00:24:55,880
and find a solution.

406
00:25:25,359 --> 00:25:27,019
Let me talk to your husband alone for a minute.

407
00:25:44,160 --> 00:25:44,940
Get out.

408
00:25:53,559 --> 00:25:54,299
I'm fine.

409
00:25:58,400 --> 00:25:58,980
Phone.

410
00:25:59,519 --> 00:26:00,259
Didn't bring it.

411
00:26:15,740 --> 00:26:16,500
Phone

412
00:26:28,180 --> 00:26:29,539
Since we know each other so well,

413
00:26:29,859 --> 00:26:31,220
I'll just get straight to the point.

414
00:26:31,640 --> 00:26:33,980
I'm in desperate need of money.

415
00:26:34,720 --> 00:26:35,500
Understood.

416
00:26:36,599 --> 00:26:38,980
We'll find a way to scrape it together.

417
00:26:44,259 --> 00:26:46,460
Save your little bit of money for baby formula.

418
00:26:47,180 --> 00:26:48,059
What do you mean?

419
00:26:48,339 --> 00:26:49,099
I

420
00:26:49,579 --> 00:26:50,539
have money.

421
00:26:51,220 --> 00:26:52,460
Millions of it.

422
00:26:53,099 --> 00:26:54,779
I just can't withdraw it right now.

423
00:26:56,099 --> 00:26:57,500
I need you to do me a favor.

424
00:26:59,500 --> 00:27:00,059
Sit.

425
00:27:00,880 --> 00:27:01,619
No need.

426
00:27:02,359 --> 00:27:03,059
What favor?

427
00:27:03,220 --> 00:27:04,339
Let me see.

428
00:27:08,000 --> 00:27:10,180
Wednesday, or Thursday works too.

429
00:27:11,220 --> 00:27:12,259
There's less traffic on those days.

430
00:27:13,099 --> 00:27:14,819
I've picked out a few options for you.

431
00:27:15,180 --> 00:27:16,180
None of them have cameras.

432
00:27:16,420 --> 00:27:17,819
And the scenery is quite nice.

433
00:27:18,839 --> 00:27:21,339
One of the spots is very close to home.

434
00:27:21,480 --> 00:27:22,500
After you're done,

435
00:27:22,619 --> 00:27:24,220
you can even come back for a meal.

436
00:27:24,759 --> 00:27:25,819
What exactly do you mean?

437
00:27:27,720 --> 00:27:28,680
It's simple.

438
00:27:29,960 --> 00:27:31,819
Come here, let me tell you.

439
00:27:32,720 --> 00:27:34,779
You'll take my wife,

440
00:27:35,599 --> 00:27:37,339
drive the car I've prepared for you,

441
00:27:37,680 --> 00:27:39,019
to the designated spot.

442
00:27:39,759 --> 00:27:41,380
But you need to check

443
00:27:42,119 --> 00:27:43,339
for any anglers

444
00:27:43,579 --> 00:27:44,980
lurking around there.

445
00:27:45,960 --> 00:27:47,299
Once you're sure it's safe,

446
00:27:48,480 --> 00:27:49,480
you'll lift my wife

447
00:27:49,940 --> 00:27:51,319
out of the car

448
00:27:52,279 --> 00:27:53,700
and lay her in the middle of the road.

449
00:27:55,180 --> 00:27:55,980
Then you'll

450
00:27:56,579 --> 00:27:58,140
back the car up a bit,

451
00:28:01,680 --> 00:28:02,539
aim it at her,

452
00:28:03,039 --> 00:28:04,579
shift into gear, hit the gas,

453
00:28:05,500 --> 00:28:07,059
and drive right over her.

454
00:28:07,799 --> 00:28:08,900
As soon as she's dead,

455
00:28:09,259 --> 00:28:10,380
the money she stole from me,

456
00:28:11,019 --> 00:28:12,299
I'll be able to get it back.

457
00:28:16,700 --> 00:28:17,700
Calm down.

458
00:28:19,440 --> 00:28:20,180
Think about it.

459
00:28:20,980 --> 00:28:22,579
From the police's perspective,

460
00:28:22,759 --> 00:28:24,380
you have absolutely no motive.

461
00:28:24,619 --> 00:28:26,059
Even if she dies,

462
00:28:26,259 --> 00:28:27,700
it won't be traced back to you.

463
00:28:27,880 --> 00:28:30,180
Why insist on rotting in prison for a decade?

464
00:28:31,380 --> 00:28:32,619
By the time you get out,

465
00:28:32,819 --> 00:28:33,859
your job will be gone.

466
00:28:34,279 --> 00:28:35,859
Your kid won't even recognize you.

467
00:28:36,160 --> 00:28:37,180
Is it really necessary?

468
00:28:39,140 --> 00:28:41,400
This is a win-win solution.

469
00:28:41,539 --> 00:28:43,460
It gets you out of trouble,

470
00:28:43,640 --> 00:28:45,380
and I get my money back.

471
00:28:45,740 --> 00:28:47,819
We can all go back to our normal lives.

472
00:28:53,720 --> 00:28:54,500
Actually,

473
00:28:54,720 --> 00:28:56,619
I can completely understand

474
00:28:57,099 --> 00:28:58,940
folks like you from small towns.

475
00:28:59,160 --> 00:29:01,059
How does that saying online go?

476
00:29:03,619 --> 00:29:06,220
Misfortune hits the weak.

477
00:29:06,880 --> 00:29:08,619
Tell me, if you were gone,

478
00:29:09,180 --> 00:29:10,579
what would your wife do all alone?

479
00:29:10,880 --> 00:29:12,339
The kid's tuition,

480
00:29:12,759 --> 00:29:14,299
the car loan, the mortgage.

481
00:29:15,000 --> 00:29:16,660
She's just a kindergarten teacher.

482
00:29:17,240 --> 00:29:18,160
Can she handle all that?

483
00:29:18,579 --> 00:29:20,099
Think about how much effort you've put in

484
00:29:20,099 --> 00:29:21,660
to build this family.

485
00:29:21,980 --> 00:29:23,940
Can you bear to watch it all vanish?

486
00:29:26,819 --> 00:29:28,220
Stop overthinking it.

487
00:29:28,660 --> 00:29:29,619
I'm telling you,

488
00:29:29,940 --> 00:29:30,900
to survive in this world,

489
00:29:31,460 --> 00:29:33,180
you just have to take a gamble.

490
00:29:37,960 --> 00:29:39,460
I'm done wasting time with you.

491
00:29:44,559 --> 00:29:45,259
Five minutes.

492
00:29:46,200 --> 00:29:47,180
Once time is up,

493
00:29:47,940 --> 00:29:49,059
you can just go to jail.

494
00:30:27,460 --> 00:30:28,299
I get it.

495
00:30:29,460 --> 00:30:31,319
You just had to waste all that time,

496
00:30:31,720 --> 00:30:33,500
only to do exactly as I say in the end?

497
00:30:33,579 --> 00:30:35,259
But there's one thing I don't get.

498
00:30:35,400 --> 00:30:36,619
How could you be so sure

499
00:30:36,619 --> 00:30:37,839
that Bai An'an is with me?

500
00:30:38,000 --> 00:30:38,400
Logically speaking,

501
00:30:38,400 --> 00:30:40,140
you shouldn't know anything at all.

502
00:30:41,400 --> 00:30:43,019
Unless you were right there at the time.

503
00:30:50,299 --> 00:30:51,539
You don't look

504
00:30:51,720 --> 00:30:52,859
so stupid after all.

505
00:30:52,920 --> 00:30:54,079
If you don't want to live here, get out!

506
00:30:54,180 --> 00:30:55,180
Go find your next one!

507
00:30:55,259 --> 00:30:56,259
Fine, I'll get out.

508
00:30:56,420 --> 00:30:57,460
Then stop the car!

509
00:31:09,500 --> 00:31:10,579
Bai An'an...

510
00:31:12,359 --> 00:31:13,299
Bai An'an!

511
00:31:19,200 --> 00:31:20,819
I'm apologizing, isn't that enough?

512
00:31:22,059 --> 00:31:22,640
Yes,

513
00:31:22,720 --> 00:31:24,299
I shouldn't have thrown a tantrum.

514
00:31:24,720 --> 00:31:25,859
And I shouldn't have hit you.

515
00:31:26,660 --> 00:31:28,420
But I was only trying to protect you.

516
00:31:29,019 --> 00:31:31,140
I hate seeing you grovel to them.

517
00:31:31,180 --> 00:31:32,460
Why put up with that humiliation?

518
00:31:33,980 --> 00:31:35,140
I'm all you need.

519
00:31:36,519 --> 00:31:38,220
Money isn't an issue for me.

520
00:31:38,539 --> 00:31:39,759
Just wait until I turn things around...

521
00:31:39,920 --> 00:31:40,779
Wang Fenqi.

522
00:31:44,980 --> 00:31:46,059
There is no future for us.

523
00:31:46,900 --> 00:31:48,220
What? What do you mean?

524
00:31:49,240 --> 00:31:50,539
I used to be just like you.

525
00:31:51,559 --> 00:31:52,859
I didn't trust anyone.

526
00:31:54,900 --> 00:31:56,660
I know exactly what my family is like.

527
00:31:59,480 --> 00:32:00,660
I was afraid to fall in love.

528
00:32:02,359 --> 00:32:03,339
Afraid to get married.

529
00:32:05,220 --> 00:32:06,819
I preferred living in denial.

530
00:32:07,619 --> 00:32:08,859
Until I met you.

531
00:32:10,140 --> 00:32:11,619
Only then was I willing to take a gamble.

532
00:32:15,819 --> 00:32:17,500
But all gamblers end up the same.

533
00:32:19,960 --> 00:32:21,220
They lose absolutely everything.

534
00:32:27,460 --> 00:32:28,140
An'an...

535
00:32:30,119 --> 00:32:31,460
You have to believe me!

536
00:32:32,019 --> 00:32:33,299
I'm definitely going to win.

537
00:32:34,960 --> 00:32:36,140
You need to stay by my side.

538
00:32:36,359 --> 00:32:37,519
Otherwise, who am I winning for?

539
00:32:37,640 --> 00:32:38,339
Right?

540
00:32:39,099 --> 00:32:39,759
You... you...

541
00:32:39,759 --> 00:32:41,619
Didn't you say it? You said...

542
00:32:42,140 --> 00:32:43,500
you'd never leave me all alone.

543
00:32:43,640 --> 00:32:45,539
You'd always be with me, right?

544
00:32:46,680 --> 00:32:48,420
You still don't understand.

545
00:32:51,740 --> 00:32:52,460
Yeah.

546
00:32:54,019 --> 00:32:55,539
You will never understand.

547
00:32:59,180 --> 00:33:01,259
Because in your world, there is only you.

548
00:33:04,099 --> 00:33:05,660
I really wanted to stay with you,

549
00:33:11,420 --> 00:33:13,180
but this is where it ends.

550
00:33:36,220 --> 00:33:37,140
Don't be afraid.

551
00:33:38,740 --> 00:33:39,740
Wang Fenqi.

552
00:35:03,480 --> 00:35:04,940
Calling me out in such a rush.

553
00:35:05,019 --> 00:35:06,219
What exactly is going on?

554
00:35:07,699 --> 00:35:09,500
What else? We had a fight.

555
00:35:09,860 --> 00:35:11,340
Slammed the car door and just left.

556
00:35:12,599 --> 00:35:13,360
I knew it.

557
00:35:13,400 --> 00:35:14,460
At this time of night...

558
00:35:14,539 --> 00:35:15,860
...it's never good news with you.

559
00:35:20,440 --> 00:35:23,659
The number you have dialed is powered off.

560
00:35:28,320 --> 00:35:31,260
The number you have dialed is power...

561
00:35:34,059 --> 00:35:35,019
Honey,

562
00:35:35,840 --> 00:35:36,739
I was wrong.

563
00:35:37,460 --> 00:35:38,739
I deeply regret it.

564
00:35:39,559 --> 00:35:41,260
I'll do my best to fix my mistakes,

565
00:35:41,500 --> 00:35:43,619
and earn back your trust.

566
00:35:56,300 --> 00:35:59,179
You've got some nerve, bro.

567
00:36:00,619 --> 00:36:02,260
Still going to work, huh?

568
00:36:03,059 --> 00:36:04,139
If you don't like it here, get out.

569
00:36:04,280 --> 00:36:05,340
Go find your next one.

570
00:36:05,420 --> 00:36:07,139
Fine, I'll get out. Stop the car!

571
00:36:08,280 --> 00:36:09,300
That night...

572
00:36:10,239 --> 00:36:11,400
my friend told me

573
00:36:11,800 --> 00:36:12,800
to go look for her.

574
00:36:13,340 --> 00:36:14,320
I told him,

575
00:36:14,719 --> 00:36:15,800
why bother looking?

576
00:36:16,079 --> 00:36:17,639
She's an adult, how could she go missing?

577
00:36:17,780 --> 00:36:18,559
I didn't expect

578
00:36:19,739 --> 00:36:21,039
that a joke like that

579
00:36:21,300 --> 00:36:22,280
would actually come true.

580
00:36:22,920 --> 00:36:24,519
Her best friend came looking for me too.

581
00:36:25,539 --> 00:36:27,480
We both thought she went back to her parents'.

582
00:36:27,639 --> 00:36:29,000
I called her for days.

583
00:36:29,000 --> 00:36:30,139
She never replied.

584
00:36:31,719 --> 00:36:33,659
I figured she must still be mad at me.

585
00:36:34,320 --> 00:36:34,980
Until...

586
00:36:36,519 --> 00:36:37,860
until my father-in-law came to the house.

587
00:36:37,900 --> 00:36:38,860
Dad, what brings you here?

588
00:36:38,860 --> 00:36:40,340
Why haven't you been answering my calls?

589
00:36:40,380 --> 00:36:41,300
That was when I realized,

590
00:36:41,780 --> 00:36:42,679
after those calls,

591
00:36:42,840 --> 00:36:44,280
that she might be in trouble.

592
00:36:45,780 --> 00:36:46,860
Officer,

593
00:36:47,320 --> 00:36:48,579
you have to help me find my wife.

594
00:36:48,579 --> 00:36:50,019
You're still putting on an act!

595
00:36:50,260 --> 00:36:50,699
What are you doing?!

596
00:36:50,699 --> 00:36:52,179
What did you do to my daughter?!

597
00:36:52,579 --> 00:36:52,900
It's okay.

598
00:36:52,900 --> 00:36:53,860
Wang Fenqi!

599
00:36:54,219 --> 00:36:55,900
What did you do to my daughter?!

600
00:36:56,179 --> 00:36:57,239
Calm down! Tell me!

601
00:36:57,239 --> 00:36:58,059
Calm down!

602
00:36:58,519 --> 00:36:59,260
Sit down first.

603
00:36:59,519 --> 00:37:00,300
Listen to us.

604
00:37:02,820 --> 00:37:03,400
Come here.

605
00:37:03,519 --> 00:37:04,480
Please calm down first.

606
00:37:15,860 --> 00:37:16,780
Officer.

607
00:37:18,900 --> 00:37:20,099
I just remembered something.

608
00:37:20,260 --> 00:37:22,099
The path where my wife and I got separated

609
00:37:22,920 --> 00:37:25,300
is only used by residents of our complex.

610
00:37:25,920 --> 00:37:27,099
You should go ask them.

611
00:37:27,380 --> 00:37:29,099
They might provide some clues.

612
00:37:55,039 --> 00:37:56,360
Under what circumstances

613
00:37:56,440 --> 00:37:57,679
is a nasogastric tube used?

614
00:37:57,820 --> 00:38:00,539
A nasogastric tube is a medical device

615
00:38:00,699 --> 00:38:03,219
inserted through the nose into the stomach or intestines.

616
00:38:03,400 --> 00:38:04,639
Its primary purpose is to

617
00:38:04,679 --> 00:38:07,820
deliver food to patients unable to eat orally.

618
00:38:15,760 --> 00:38:17,940
That idiot's actually trying to save her.

619
00:38:33,260 --> 00:38:34,059
Let me go!

620
00:38:34,400 --> 00:38:35,460
What are you doing?

621
00:38:35,739 --> 00:38:36,500
Settle down!

622
00:38:37,360 --> 00:38:39,420
He's the one who pushed me!

623
00:38:41,079 --> 00:38:42,880
You have to arrest him!

624
00:38:42,960 --> 00:38:44,300
Officer!

625
00:39:12,099 --> 00:39:12,820
Come here.

626
00:39:15,539 --> 00:39:16,260
Come here.

627
00:39:18,320 --> 00:39:19,420
I said, come here!

628
00:39:49,599 --> 00:39:51,340
If anything happens to her,

629
00:39:51,659 --> 00:39:52,539
I'll scour the earth

630
00:39:52,539 --> 00:39:54,219
to dig that bastard out.

631
00:39:54,579 --> 00:39:55,900
I'll trade my life for his.

632
00:39:56,039 --> 00:39:57,619
I'll make him wish he was dead.

633
00:40:02,900 --> 00:40:05,400
Hurry up and do it, idiot!

634
00:40:19,599 --> 00:40:21,679
Where the hell are they hiding?

635
00:40:32,019 --> 00:40:34,139
Did you take the wrong package again?

636
00:40:34,400 --> 00:40:35,820
Can I come in and take a look?

637
00:40:45,079 --> 00:40:46,179
If there's a real problem, call 110.

638
00:40:46,300 --> 00:40:47,380
I'll open the door as soon as the police arrive.

639
00:40:47,460 --> 00:40:48,059
Okay?

640
00:40:51,880 --> 00:40:53,780
As of right now, the principal

641
00:40:53,860 --> 00:40:56,460
has accumulated into quite a large sum.

642
00:40:57,260 --> 00:41:00,699
Unless she were to pass away.

643
00:41:01,219 --> 00:41:03,360
Then, as the primary heir,

644
00:41:03,420 --> 00:41:05,739
it wouldn't just be about the principal.

645
00:41:07,360 --> 00:41:09,420
You'd also get the insurance payout.

646
00:41:27,139 --> 00:41:30,059
She suddenly appeared on the road.

647
00:41:30,219 --> 00:41:32,179
It was like someone pushed her.

648
00:41:34,539 --> 00:41:35,659
You don't look

649
00:41:35,900 --> 00:41:37,300
that stupid after all.

650
00:41:40,579 --> 00:41:41,940
So all this time,

651
00:41:42,019 --> 00:41:43,420
it was because of you

652
00:41:43,460 --> 00:41:44,719
that I became your... taking the fall...

653
00:41:44,719 --> 00:41:46,980
Don't make it sound so ugly.

654
00:41:48,820 --> 00:41:50,420
If you were so honorable,

655
00:41:50,659 --> 00:41:52,780
you wouldn't have ended up like this.

656
00:41:52,860 --> 00:41:54,780
If you had taken her to the hospital back then

657
00:41:54,940 --> 00:41:55,980
and waited for her to wake up,

658
00:41:56,659 --> 00:41:58,260
wouldn't everything be clear?

659
00:41:58,519 --> 00:41:59,460
But you didn't.

660
00:42:00,940 --> 00:42:02,179
You chose to save yourself.

661
00:42:05,159 --> 00:42:06,059
I just...

662
00:42:06,199 --> 00:42:08,179
But you didn't go all the way.

663
00:42:09,880 --> 00:42:11,579
Hesitating,

664
00:42:11,940 --> 00:42:13,780
only to waste away here.

665
00:42:14,619 --> 00:42:15,579
Right?

666
00:42:18,960 --> 00:42:20,380
You should thank me.

667
00:42:21,099 --> 00:42:23,380
You should get on your knees and thank me

668
00:42:25,360 --> 00:42:28,139
for cleaning up this mess for you.

669
00:42:29,300 --> 00:42:31,260
W-What are you talking about?

670
00:42:35,139 --> 00:42:37,219
That woman is your wife.

671
00:42:41,940 --> 00:42:43,300
I gave her a chance.

672
00:42:44,820 --> 00:42:46,460
She didn't appreciate it.

673
00:42:47,199 --> 00:42:48,260
I used to think

674
00:42:48,840 --> 00:42:51,300
she was the only one in the world who understood me.

675
00:42:54,059 --> 00:42:55,139
But in the end?

676
00:42:57,579 --> 00:42:58,820
She's just like the rest of you.

677
00:42:59,239 --> 00:43:00,900
Just a cowardly,

678
00:43:01,039 --> 00:43:02,300
untrustworthy,

679
00:43:02,460 --> 00:43:04,139
and a mediocre fool.

680
00:43:05,699 --> 00:43:06,780
I don't need her.

681
00:43:08,420 --> 00:43:09,739
I'm enough for myself.

682
00:43:17,239 --> 00:43:18,139
Wang Fenqi.

683
00:43:19,000 --> 00:43:20,380
You were married.

684
00:43:22,380 --> 00:43:24,820
Don't you feel any guilt at all?

685
00:43:33,579 --> 00:43:35,099
I almost laughed out loud back then.

686
00:43:35,099 --> 00:43:36,019
You know?

687
00:43:36,440 --> 00:43:37,599
I was actually quite worried.

688
00:43:37,820 --> 00:43:39,079
I thought you saw me.

689
00:43:39,659 --> 00:43:40,699
But I didn't expect

690
00:43:41,179 --> 00:43:42,079
you'd freeze in fear.

691
00:43:42,940 --> 00:43:44,179
Hesitating,

692
00:43:44,739 --> 00:43:46,000
too scared to even run.

693
00:43:46,519 --> 00:43:47,960
And finally, trembling,

694
00:43:47,960 --> 00:43:49,480
you carried her into the car.

695
00:43:51,000 --> 00:43:52,639
What can I say?

696
00:43:53,900 --> 00:43:56,039
Fate is always on my side.

697
00:43:57,280 --> 00:43:58,559
That's fate.

698
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:01,579
You have to accept it.

699
00:44:06,219 --> 00:44:07,280
You're right.

700
00:44:11,079 --> 00:44:11,840
I was wrong.

701
00:44:12,099 --> 00:44:12,780
I have to accept it.

702
00:44:14,159 --> 00:44:15,920
I will turn myself in to the police.

703
00:44:17,159 --> 00:44:18,579
I'll confess everything.

704
00:44:28,940 --> 00:44:30,179
We're neighbors.

705
00:44:30,639 --> 00:44:31,940
Why did it have to come to this?

706
00:44:32,119 --> 00:44:34,139
Why did you have to make things so unpleasant?

707
00:44:36,440 --> 00:44:38,300
Couldn't you just make it easy?

708
00:44:38,900 --> 00:44:39,820
Well, now look.

709
00:44:40,860 --> 00:44:42,380
I have to finish you two off first,

710
00:44:42,940 --> 00:44:44,980
then kill my wife with my own hands.

711
00:44:45,119 --> 00:44:46,239
What are you talking about?

712
00:44:46,559 --> 00:44:48,380
After the police arrive,

713
00:44:48,519 --> 00:44:51,320
I'll have to put on quite an act.

714
00:44:51,760 --> 00:44:53,480
Wang Fenqi, what are you doing?

715
00:44:55,679 --> 00:44:57,179
Why don't you really...

716
00:44:57,920 --> 00:44:59,380
...really think this through?

717
00:45:00,400 --> 00:45:01,079
Wang Fenqi!

718
00:45:01,219 --> 00:45:02,900
Wang Fenqi, you... you...

719
00:45:02,940 --> 00:45:03,820
Just calm down.

720
00:45:03,900 --> 00:45:04,940
Listen to me.

721
00:45:05,260 --> 00:45:07,300
I'm not a murderer, and neither are you.

722
00:45:08,340 --> 00:45:10,420
We both still have a chance to start over.

723
00:45:11,480 --> 00:45:12,380
Listen to me.

724
00:45:13,320 --> 00:45:15,139
Your wife isn't dead yet.

725
00:45:27,820 --> 00:45:28,860
Bai An'an

726
00:45:52,380 --> 00:45:53,380
Don't be scared.

727
00:45:54,940 --> 00:45:55,739
I promise you,

728
00:45:57,099 --> 00:45:58,780
we won't hurt you.

729
00:45:58,900 --> 00:46:00,380
we won't hurt you.

730
00:46:01,820 --> 00:46:03,260
I know you don't trust me,

731
00:46:03,460 --> 00:46:06,380
but I'll do anything to make up for this.

732
00:46:07,059 --> 00:46:08,340
Whatever you ask for,

733
00:46:08,500 --> 00:46:09,380
we'll accept it.

734
00:46:09,940 --> 00:46:11,179
we'll accept it.

735
00:46:12,960 --> 00:46:13,900
Even going to the police.

736
00:46:17,119 --> 00:46:18,699
I don't need your compensation.

737
00:46:20,679 --> 00:46:22,179
I just want Wang Fenqi

738
00:46:23,980 --> 00:46:25,019
to pay the price.

739
00:46:29,260 --> 00:46:30,460
Will you help me?

740
00:46:31,619 --> 00:46:34,059
But in your current condition,

741
00:46:35,039 --> 00:46:36,820
doing this is way too risky.

742
00:46:37,460 --> 00:46:38,260
It doesn't matter.

743
00:46:40,139 --> 00:46:41,019
It's the only way

744
00:46:41,940 --> 00:46:44,260
you can be free from all this.

745
00:46:45,559 --> 00:46:47,619
And the only way I can truly start over.

746
00:46:55,380 --> 00:46:56,579
We can't drag this out anymore.

747
00:46:56,920 --> 00:46:57,980
He'll get suspicious.

748
00:46:58,940 --> 00:47:00,340
Remember what we just talked about.

749
00:47:02,380 --> 00:47:03,980
The more he sees you suffer,

750
00:47:04,920 --> 00:47:06,099
the more smug he'll get,

751
00:47:07,019 --> 00:47:08,420
and the more he'll run his mouth.

752
00:47:10,159 --> 00:47:12,260
When he thinks he's already won

753
00:47:14,519 --> 00:47:16,260
is when he'll let his guard down.

754
00:47:20,940 --> 00:47:22,420
No one loses forever.

755
00:47:24,000 --> 00:47:25,739
And no one wins forever.

756
00:47:28,800 --> 00:47:30,179
Where did she go?

757
00:47:30,380 --> 00:47:32,219
Don't panic. She couldn't have gone far.

758
00:47:32,860 --> 00:47:34,340
You take the east gate, I'll take the west.

759
00:48:08,460 --> 00:48:09,500
I don't need her.

760
00:48:11,199 --> 00:48:12,539
I'm all I need.

761
00:48:14,260 --> 00:48:15,659
You were married, after all.

762
00:48:16,260 --> 00:48:18,500
Don't you feel any guilt at all?

763
00:48:22,739 --> 00:48:24,219
I almost laughed out loud.

764
00:48:24,219 --> 00:48:25,139
You know what?

765
00:48:25,599 --> 00:48:26,820
I was really worried at first.

766
00:48:26,980 --> 00:48:28,260
I thought you saw me.

767
00:48:30,280 --> 00:48:31,380
Bai An'an!

768
00:48:32,460 --> 00:48:33,420
Bai An'an!

769
00:48:33,579 --> 00:48:35,219
Open the door! Open the door!

770
00:48:36,400 --> 00:48:37,300
Open the door!

771
00:48:38,320 --> 00:48:39,019
Open the door!

772
00:48:53,820 --> 00:48:54,380
Come.

773
00:49:29,059 --> 00:49:30,480
If you don't come out,

774
00:49:31,139 --> 00:49:33,840
I'll beat Dr. Ma to death.

775
00:49:39,500 --> 00:49:40,820
Send the video out first.

776
00:50:58,159 --> 00:50:59,780
The video's been sent.

777
00:51:00,000 --> 00:51:01,059
You're not getting away.

778
00:51:05,619 --> 00:51:06,780
We'll see about that.

779
00:51:22,519 --> 00:51:23,320
Move!

780
00:51:24,719 --> 00:51:25,519
Move!

781
00:53:14,260 --> 00:53:14,960
Let me tell you,

782
00:53:14,960 --> 00:53:16,699
I have no trouble finding tenants here.

783
00:53:16,840 --> 00:53:17,940
Take it or leave it.

784
00:53:18,420 --> 00:53:18,960
After all these years,

785
00:53:18,960 --> 00:53:20,500
I've met all kinds of people,

786
00:53:20,880 --> 00:53:22,340
and I've seen it all.

787
00:53:40,500 --> 00:53:41,579
What happened?

788
00:53:42,039 --> 00:53:43,739
Just a little disagreement between neighbors.

789
00:54:02,980 --> 00:54:04,360
The first story I want to share

790
00:54:04,400 --> 00:54:05,880
is from a girl's submission.

791
00:54:05,960 --> 00:54:06,980
She said she encountered an

792
00:54:07,019 --> 00:54:08,519
extremely obnoxious neighbor.

793
00:54:15,159 --> 00:54:16,260
Stop following me!

794
00:54:17,039 --> 00:54:18,059
Go find your husband.

795
00:54:18,940 --> 00:54:20,099
Go scroll through your videos.

796
00:54:21,119 --> 00:54:22,099
Go watch your livestreams.

797
00:54:31,400 --> 00:54:32,320
What's going on here?

798
00:54:32,380 --> 00:54:33,360
I don't know. I just got off work.

799
00:54:33,420 --> 00:54:34,480
Better call an ambulance.

800
00:54:35,239 --> 00:54:36,039
You call them.

801
00:54:36,360 --> 00:54:37,920
I saw them from my window just now.

802
00:54:38,000 --> 00:54:39,360
They were chasing each other for quite a while.

803
00:54:40,000 --> 00:54:41,420
Did you... did you get that on video?

804
00:54:41,519 --> 00:54:43,079
Stop filming and call the police!

805
00:54:43,519 --> 00:54:44,559
They're still breathing!

806
00:54:44,900 --> 00:54:45,760
Better call an ambulance.

807
00:54:45,760 --> 00:54:46,940
Building management! Call management!

808
00:54:51,039 --> 00:54:53,000
Out of respect for our time as neighbors,

809
00:54:54,579 --> 00:54:57,079
can't we just part on good terms?

810
00:54:58,199 --> 00:54:59,320
Respect?

811
00:55:02,559 --> 00:55:04,320
That's reserved for human beings.

812
00:55:17,940 --> 00:55:18,820
Please come quickly!

813
00:55:19,400 --> 00:55:20,260
1... 102.

814
00:55:20,300 --> 00:55:20,980
101.

815
00:55:26,340 --> 00:55:27,619
What exactly happened to you?

816
00:55:27,780 --> 00:55:28,360
Are you okay?

817
00:55:28,360 --> 00:55:29,300
Please...

818
00:55:29,860 --> 00:55:31,179
...help me call an ambulance.

819
00:55:31,460 --> 00:55:32,139
I did, I did.

820
00:55:32,219 --> 00:55:34,059
My neighbor is seriously injured.

821
00:55:36,019 --> 00:55:36,860
I'll go in and take a look.

822
00:55:36,960 --> 00:55:37,940
Hang in there.

823
00:55:42,699 --> 00:55:43,380
Buddy.

824
00:55:44,619 --> 00:55:45,260
Buddy.

825
00:55:46,820 --> 00:55:47,500
Buddy.

826
00:55:47,960 --> 00:55:48,659
Are you okay?

827
00:55:48,900 --> 00:55:49,699
Hang in there!

828
00:55:49,940 --> 00:55:51,280
Bro, bro, stop shaking me. Hang in there.

829
00:55:51,280 --> 00:55:52,500
Okay, okay, okay.

830
00:55:52,659 --> 00:55:53,539
I've called an ambulance.

831
00:55:53,659 --> 00:55:54,500
Just hang in there.

832
00:55:54,659 --> 00:55:56,500
I might pass out soon.

833
00:55:56,820 --> 00:55:58,940
Please tell the paramedics for me...

834
00:55:59,380 --> 00:56:00,539
...that the injuries on my face and body...

835
00:56:00,619 --> 00:56:02,539
...are mostly contusions and bruises.

836
00:56:02,599 --> 00:56:03,420
They're not a big deal.

837
00:56:03,699 --> 00:56:06,500
But my skull was repeatedly struck by a hard object.

838
00:56:06,699 --> 00:56:09,380
First, rule out epidural and subdural hematoma.

839
00:56:09,719 --> 00:56:10,420
At a time like this...

840
00:56:10,460 --> 00:56:11,420
...let's not talk about that.

841
00:56:11,739 --> 00:56:12,619
Save your breath.

842
00:56:12,800 --> 00:56:14,460
I'll ask them where they are, okay?

843
00:56:18,300 --> 00:56:19,059
Bro.

844
00:56:20,420 --> 00:56:21,780
I see you around all the time...

845
00:56:22,539 --> 00:56:24,820
...but I still don't know your name.

846
00:57:21,559 --> 00:57:22,440
I saw the whole thing.

847
00:57:22,480 --> 00:57:23,400
That was completely out of line.

848
00:57:23,500 --> 00:57:24,460
It's absolutely appalling.

849
00:57:24,659 --> 00:57:25,860
Scared my kid half to death.

850
00:57:25,980 --> 00:57:27,340
Too terrified to even cry.

851
00:57:27,460 --> 00:57:28,840
He wasn't acting?

852
00:57:29,039 --> 00:57:30,280
I thought it was an act.

853
00:57:30,760 --> 00:57:32,039
Let's go. Back to sleep.

854
00:57:32,239 --> 00:57:32,800
I'm going back to my game.

855
00:57:32,800 --> 00:57:33,840
Let's go, let's go.

856
00:58:15,900 --> 00:58:16,780
Just a minute.

857
00:58:16,880 --> 00:58:17,900
I'll be right there.

858
00:58:20,739 --> 00:58:21,820
The landlord is traveling,

859
00:58:21,940 --> 00:58:22,860
so I'll open the door for you.

860
00:58:23,440 --> 00:58:24,179
Thank you.

861
00:58:27,519 --> 00:58:28,800
Welcome home.

862
00:58:32,320 --> 00:58:33,800
The living room is so spacious.

863
00:58:34,039 --> 00:58:35,079
And the lighting is great!

864
00:58:35,159 --> 00:58:36,039
We can put up a partition here,

865
00:58:36,579 --> 00:58:37,519
and build that mini bar you've always wanted.

866
00:58:37,639 --> 00:58:38,159
Yes, that sounds great!

867
00:58:38,380 --> 00:58:39,960
Your design computer can go here too.

868
00:58:40,079 --> 00:58:41,619
No need, it's still huge inside.

869
00:58:41,860 --> 00:58:42,960
I feel like this is the one, honey.

870
00:58:42,960 --> 00:58:44,239
I told you, keep your voice down.

871
00:58:44,280 --> 00:58:45,219
How do you like it?

872
00:58:45,840 --> 00:58:46,880
We're both extremely satisfied.

873
00:58:47,099 --> 00:58:48,139
And that fire escape...

874
00:58:48,260 --> 00:58:49,920
Honey, after the baby is born,

875
00:58:50,059 --> 00:58:51,119
we can play hide-and-seek together.

876
00:58:52,719 --> 00:58:53,400
Miss,

877
00:58:54,039 --> 00:58:56,760
I know you must be close with the landlord.

878
00:58:56,900 --> 00:58:57,559
Do you think...

879
00:58:57,820 --> 00:59:00,019
you could help us negotiate the price a bit?

880
00:59:00,639 --> 00:59:02,800
My husband just changed jobs recently,

881
00:59:03,239 --> 00:59:05,760
and I just happened to find out I'm pregnant.

882
00:59:06,719 --> 00:59:09,360
So things are pretty tight financially.

883
00:59:09,760 --> 00:59:10,400
You see,

884
00:59:10,659 --> 00:59:12,219
there's the mortgage, the car loan,

885
00:59:12,300 --> 00:59:13,659
renovation costs, gas money,

886
00:59:13,659 --> 00:59:15,340
HOA fees, utility bills...

887
00:59:16,000 --> 00:59:17,239
Then there's the delivery room,

888
00:59:17,300 --> 00:59:19,079
a nanny, formula, diapers...

889
00:59:19,800 --> 00:59:20,800
When the child gets a bit older,

890
00:59:20,880 --> 00:59:22,159
we have to consider extracurricular classes.

891
00:59:23,059 --> 00:59:24,500
Our families are in decent health for now,

892
00:59:25,019 --> 00:59:26,380
but we have to plan for that later too.

893
00:59:28,280 --> 00:59:30,099
Everyone charges forward while drumming up their courage.

894
00:59:30,579 --> 00:59:31,880
After all, living in constant terror

895
00:59:32,139 --> 00:59:33,400
won't bring you any comfort.

896
00:59:34,019 --> 00:59:35,019
Begging on your knees

897
00:59:35,840 --> 00:59:37,500
won't make anyone show mercy.

898
00:59:38,360 --> 00:59:40,219
There is nothing truly worth fearing.

899
00:59:41,539 --> 00:59:43,219
Just march forward with your head held high.

900
00:59:44,639 --> 00:59:45,539
When you look back,

901
00:59:46,719 --> 00:59:48,159
you'll see it's really no big deal.

902
00:59:48,619 --> 00:59:49,400
Don't be afraid.

903
00:59:50,199 --> 00:59:51,280
It will all pass.

904
00:59:55,559 --> 00:59:56,820
Once we actually become neighbors,

905
00:59:57,280 --> 00:59:59,340
I'll tell you our story sometime.
